1
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:18,888
Henry Ford was born on a farm near Dearborn, Michigan, in eighteen sixty-three. As a boy, he cared far more about machines than about farm work.

2
00:00:19,538 --> 00:00:32,908
In eighteen ninety-six, he built his first gasoline-powered vehicle, the Quadricycle. In nineteen oh-three, he started the Ford Motor Company.

3
00:00:33,558 --> 00:00:44,288
The Model T arrived in nineteen oh-eight. It was built for ordinary families, and about fifteen million of them were made.

4
00:00:44,938 --> 00:01:02,068
In nineteen thirteen, his factory began building cars on a moving assembly line. A chassis that once took about twelve and a half hours could be finished in about ninety-three minutes.

5
00:01:02,718 --> 00:01:17,128
In nineteen fourteen, Ford announced a five-dollar day, far above the usual pay. But to earn the full bonus, workers had to follow his rules about how they lived at home.

6
00:01:17,778 --> 00:01:42,268
Ford also owned a newspaper, The Dearborn Independent. In nineteen twenty, it began a long series of articles blaming Jewish people for the world's problems. The series used a forged document, and it spread hatred.

7
00:01:42,918 --> 00:01:56,097
In nineteen twenty-seven, after a lawsuit, Ford publicly apologized. Historians still disagree about how much he knew of the articles, and what he meant by the apology.

8
00:01:56,747 --> 00:02:08,337
At the Rouge plant in nineteen thirty-seven, Ford's security men beat union organizers. Ford did not sign a contract with the union until nineteen forty-one.

9
00:02:08,987 --> 00:02:25,708
In nineteen thirty-eight, Ford accepted a high Nazi honor, the Grand Cross of the German Eagle. Yet in the Second World War, his Willow Run factory built B-24 bombers for the United States.

10
00:02:26,358 --> 00:02:42,768
Henry Ford died in nineteen forty-seven, at his home, Fair Lane. Historians still disagree about how to weigh his achievements against his hatred, and his treatment of workers.

